    "ImageDescription": {
      "value": "A 14th-century depiction of the 11th century <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Almoravid_dynasty\">Almoravid</a> general <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abu%20Bakr%20ibn%20Umar\">Abu Bakr ibn Umar</a> (\"Rex Bubecar\") near the Senegal River, from the book Catalan Atlas of 1375 AD. Abu Bakr was known for his conquests in Africa. \n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanhaja\">Sanhaja Berbers</a>, who created the Almoravid empire, were known as 'the veiled ones' due to their custom of wearing a face veil.<sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\nCaption: \"All this land is populated by people who cover themselves such that only their eyes can be seen; they live in tents and ride in camels. There are animals named lemp [orice] whose skin can be used to make good leather shields.\" <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.cresquesproject.net/catalan-atlas-legends/panel-iii\">https://www.cresquesproject.net/catalan-atlas-legends/panel-iii</a>",
